      <!-- Right: accordion list -->
      <div class="faq-list reveal">
        <details class="faq-item" open data-faq-item>
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q-index">Q1</span>
            <span class="faq-q">How does an engagement with Platform Play Venture typically begin?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>The process usually begins with understanding the current position of the brand, the decisions being made today, and what the business is trying to achieve next. The first step focuses on identifying gaps in clarity and direction before defining the right strategic path forward.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" data-faq-item>
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q-index">Q2</span>
            <span class="faq-q">What happens after the strategy is defined?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Our role does not end at strategy. Platform Play Venture stays involved in guiding direction, supporting leadership and marketing teams in decision-making, and ensuring that the strategy translates into consistent progress over time.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" data-faq-item>
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q-index">Q3</span>
            <span class="faq-q">How does Platform Play Venture work alongside internal teams?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>The approach is collaborative. The focus is on strengthening clarity, improving alignment, and helping internal teams operate with a clearer sense of direction rather than replacing what already exists.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" data-faq-item>
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q-index">Q4</span>
            <span class="faq-q">At what stage of a brand does working with PPV make the most sense?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>It works best when a business is growing but feels that marketing efforts are not fully aligned with business goals, or when the brand is entering a new phase and needs clearer direction before scaling further.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" data-faq-item>
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q-index">Q5</span>
            <span class="faq-q">What can a brand realistically expect after working with Platform Play Venture?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>The biggest change is usually clarity. Businesses start understanding what to prioritise, what to avoid, and how different parts of marketing, technology, and brand perception should work together. That clarity makes future decisions faster and more confident.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" data-faq-item>
          <summary>
            <span class="faq-q-index">Q6</span>
            <span class="faq-q">What does working with a fractional CMO actually mean?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>A fractional CMO means working with an experienced strategic partner who supports leadership and marketing teams in planning, decision-making, and guiding marketing direction — without the need for a full-time in-house CMO. The role is senior, embedded, and accountable to outcomes, not headcount.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
